Actually, one important thing is my profiles/radiance etc are in .mat
files ... I assume they can be read in by Python? I heard they have to
be separate variabes, and not lumped together in a structure

Yes, Python can read .mat files, and what you heard is basically right
— it's much less painful if you save flat variables rather than a
struct.  The core tool is scipy.io.loadmat, but there's a version
split that matters:

v7 and earlier (the default unless you use -v7.3): scipy.io.loadmat
works directly, returns a dict.  v7.3 (HDF5-based — Matlab switches to
this automatically for variables over 2GB, or if you explicitly
save(..., '-v7.3')): scipy.io.loadmat cannot read these. You need h5py
or the mat73 package instead.

Check which you have — if scipy.io.loadmat throws an error like
NotImplementedError: Please use HDF reader for matlab v7.3 files,
that's your answer.

